#
# Once a day (setup.py daily): the Web Application Firewall's audit and error logs' day files older than
# OPNsense keeps its own logs (System: Settings: Logging, Preserve logs, 31 days by default) taken away;
# then, while it is on and Apache runs, each certificate Apache serves compared with System: Trust's - one
# renewed there (os-acme-client renews them in place, and OPNsense tells no plugin) is written again and
# Apache reloaded gracefully with it, nothing else of its configuration changed. Otherwise it lists two
# directories, reads config.xml once and contacts no one. In /usr/local/etc/cron.d, as the family's other
# plugins: OPNsense writes its own crontab again from its own jobs.

17 4 * * * root /usr/local/opnsense/scripts/modsecurity/setup.py daily > /dev/null 2>&1
